    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "By the in-ter-ces-sions of Thy Mar-tyrs, O Lord, grant rest un-to the souls of Thy ser-vants.\n\nIn the ce-les-tial bride-cham-bers, the no-ble choirs of the Mar-tyrs cease-less-ly make ap-peal to Thee, O Christ: Grant that all who kept the Faith whom Thou hast trans-lat-ed from the earth find all e-ter-nal__ good.__\n\nTheir souls shall dwell a-mong good__ things.\n\nSet-ting all things in fair or-der, Thou mad-est me, man, a min-gled an-i-mal, half ab-ject and half au-gust. Hence, we make re-quest of Thee: O Sav-iour, be-stow e-ter-nal rest up-on Thy ser-vants’__ souls.__\n\nGlo-ry to the Fa-ther, and to the Son, and to the Ho--ly Spir-it.\n\nThou first didst make me the cit-i-zen and the chief hus-band-man of Par-a-dise; but when I broke Thy com-mand, Thou didst ban-ish me there-from. O Sav-iour, be-stow e-ter-nal rest up-on Thy ser-vants’__ souls.__\n\nBoth now and ev--er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nHe that formed Eve, our first fore-moth-er, from a rib, wrapped Him-self a-bout with flesh from thy pure and spot-less womb; and by means of that same flesh, O Vir-gin, He ut-ter-ly de-stroyed the force and strength of__ death.__"
    }
